/-!
BLOCKCOMPLETE (LEANBLOCK, Nov 20).  Kernel-only (no native_decide / sorry / new axioms).
Imports Nov15.FrameCert (olean built with runlean.sh).  COMPLETENESS of the 1152-list:
  every 2-dim normal subspace {a,b,a^b} of F2^9 (43435 of them) is either one of FrameCert.certs or has a
  witness frame disjoint from Lam(a,b); a "blocking 7-dim section" (meets every one of the 759 frames) is
  therefore listed:  block_complete.
Certificate: dat = 43435 packed entries  a + 512*(b + 512*w),  w < 759 a frame index with frame & Lam = 0,
  or w = 1000+i with certs[i] = (a,b).  Check is linear in the candidate count.
Coverage of dat over ALL canonical pairs (a<b<a^b) is checked as a list equality of keys.
-/
